======================================================================
KEY STATISTICAL COMPARISONS (Low-Margin vs Normal Orders)
======================================================================

--- Sales Quantity ---
Low-Margin:  mean=6.72, median=5.0, std=6.22
Normal:      mean=53.18, median=53.0, std=26.89
Mann-Whitney U test: p-value = 0.00e+00 (significant difference)

--- Discount Rate (% of List Price) ---
Low-Margin:  mean=21.66%, median=11.92%
Normal:      mean=1.41%, median=0.74%
Mann-Whitney U test: p-value = 0.00e+00 (significant difference)

--- Cost per Unit ($) ---
Low-Margin:  mean=33.51, median=21.88
Normal:      mean=2.83, median=1.77
Mann-Whitney U test: p-value = 0.00e+00 (significant difference)

--- Revenue per Unit ($) ---
Low-Margin:  mean=23.49, median=18.19
Normal:      mean=28.58, median=28.87
Mann-Whitney U test: p-value = 2.12e-52 (significant difference)

--- Freight Cost per Unit ($) ---
Low-Margin:  mean=20.03, median=12.33
Normal:      mean=1.64, median=1.04


--- Cost Structure Analysis: Correlation with Quantity ---
Low-Margin: Cost vs Quantity correlation r = 0.2580
Normal:     Cost vs Quantity correlation r = 0.0338
Low-Margin: Rev vs Quantity correlation r = 0.6041
Normal:     Rev vs Quantity correlation r = 0.6812


